{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PgrQV8gmbcFbn8KiW24kVc","type":"tool_result","content":"# Step 1 notes\n\n## Change\n`router.py` now returns `fees_fx` for exchange-rate complaints. In all other cases it returns Laya's answer.\n\n## Rules (any one triggers fees_fx)\n1. \"exchange rate\" (typos such as \"exhange\" are allowed), \"currency rate\", \"conversion rate\" or \"fx rate\".\n2. A bare \"rate\" together with a complaint word (wrong, incorrect, bad, error, correct, applied, interbank, and others).\n3. \"wrong amount\" (or the typo \"wing amount\") for an item or a purchase.\n4. ATM or cash, plus a currency, plus a cost, fee, charge or rate.\n\nThe rules apply whatever Laya answered. By the department descriptions, exchange rates always belong to fees_fx.\n\n## Earlier corrections\nNone existed.\n\n## Checks\n- `evidence.csv`: 32/32 correct.\n- 12 negative messages I wrote (double charge, wrong ATM cash amount, declined payment, top-up, and others): 12/12 keep Laya's answer.\n\n## Risks\n- Rule 3 can catch a real dispute such as \"wrong amount for an item\" when no currency is involved.\n- Rule 4 can catch a cards question about using a card abroad.\nEdit `router.py` so the final answers follow the new correction for all such\nmessages, keep earlier corrections, and otherwise keep Laya's answer. Plain Python\nonly (re, string ops); no ML libraries, no training. A hidden test set scores it.\nTo test your patch, use this Python: `<lab>/.venv/bin/python`.\nWrite `NOTES.md` (under 200 words).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec87612-5b1e-4b65-b02c-f96704c7f1f8","uuid":"62133ff5-7b5d-4395-bce0-41cd56a8f64b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:23:44.744Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Step 1 notes\n\n## Change\n`router.py` now returns `fees_fx` for exchange-rate complaints. In all other cases it returns Laya's answer.\n\n## Rules (any one triggers fees_fx)\n1. \"exchange rate\" (typos such as \"exhange\" are allowed), \"currency rate\", \"conversion rate\" or \"fx rate\".\n2. A bare \"rate\" together with a complaint word (wrong, incorrect, bad, error, correct, applied, interbank, and others).\n3. \"wrong amount\" (or the typo \"wing amount\") for an item or a purchase.\n4. ATM or cash, plus a currency, plus a cost, fee, charge or rate.\n\nThe rules apply whatever Laya answered. By the department descriptions, exchange rates always belong to fees_fx.\n\n## Earlier corrections\nNone existed.\n\n## Checks\n- `evidence.csv`: 32/32 correct.\n- 12 negative messages I wrote (double charge, wrong ATM cash amount, declined payment, top-up, and others): 12/12 keep Laya's answer.\n\n## Risks\n- Rule 3 can catch a real dispute such as \"wrong amount for an item\" when no currency is involved.\n- Rule 4 can catch a cards question about using a card abroad.\nEdit `router.py` so the final answers follow the new correction for all such\nmessages, keep earlier corrections, and otherwise keep Laya's answer. Plain Python\nonly (re, string ops); no ML libraries, no training. A hidden test set scores it.\nTo test your patch, use this Python: `<lab>/.venv/bin/python`.\nWrite `NOTES.md` (under 200 words).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PgrQV8gmbcFbn8KiW24kVc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
