{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiCT3NdfyASUzQACuF2W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SmThEQyppibRQTuo3MWcA1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s0/opus-high-code-r2/step2/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 2 notes\n\n## Change\n`router.py` now sends card-PIN messages to `cards`. In all other cases it keeps the step 1 rule, then Laya's answer.\n\n## Order\n1. Step 1 exchange-rate rule runs first. An exchange-rate complaint that mentions a PIN still goes to `fees_fx`.\n2. PIN rule runs second.\n\n## PIN rule\n- The word PIN (also \"pins\", \"pin code\", \"pin number\", \"P.I.N.\", \"personal identification number\"), and Laya answered `account_security`: go to `cards`.\n- Same word, and Laya answered `disputes`: go to `cards` only if the PIN itself is the problem (blocked, changed, reset, wrong, tries, and others). \"A payment made without my PIN\" stays a dispute.\n- No PIN word, but \"too many tries\" or \"all my attempts\", and Laya answered `account_security`: go to `cards`, unless the message says passcode or password.\n- Other Laya answers (for example `fees_fx` for \"fee to change my PIN\") stay.\n\n## Checks\nCommand: `python t.py step2/router.py step2/evidence.csv step1/evidence.csv` (test script in my scratchpad).\n- Step 2 evidence: 32/32.\n- Step 1 evidence: 32/32 (earlier correction kept).\n- 12 hand-written negatives (passcode, identity, lost phone, PIN with exchange rate, and others): 12/12.\n\n## Risks\n- A PIN message that Laya sends to `transfers_topups` or `fees_fx` does not move.\n- \"Too many tries\" without \"PIN\" can catch a passcode lockout that does not say \"passcode\".\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1260,"cache_read_input_tokens":68345,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":126